# Admin App — Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values before running the app.

## Required in all environments

```env
# iron-session cookie encryption key.
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Minimum 32 characters. NEVER commit this value.
AUTH_SECRET=

# Auth mode: "mock" for development only, "external" for production.
# Validation will hard-fail if AUTH_MODE=mock is set in NODE_ENV=production.
AUTH_MODE=mock

# Prisma database connection string.
# SQLite (development):
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"
# PostgreSQL (production):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/cis_kenya_admin"
```

## Required when AUTH_MODE=external

```env
# Base URL of the external auth provider (no trailing slash).
# Example: https://auth.yourdomain.com
EXTERNAL_AUTH_URL=
```

## Optional

```env
# Mock mode credentials (only used when AUTH_MODE=mock).
# Defaults: admin / admin123
MOCK_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
MOCK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin123

# Session cookie lifetime in seconds. Default: 28800 (8 hours).
SESSION_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=28800
```

---

## Vercel deployment

Set the following in the Vercel dashboard under **Settings → Environment Variables**:

| Variable            | Required | Notes                                              |
|---------------------|----------|----------------------------------------------------|
| `AUTH_SECRET`       | ✅ Always | Min 32 chars; use Vercel's Secret store            |
| `AUTH_MODE`         | ✅ Always | Must be `external` in production                   |
| `DATABASE_URL`      | ✅ Always | PostgreSQL connection string for production        |
| `EXTERNAL_AUTH_URL` | ✅ Prod   | Required when `AUTH_MODE=external`                 |
| `SESSION_MAX_AGE_SECONDS` | No | Defaults to 28800 (8 h)                      |

> ⚠️ **Never** set `AUTH_MODE=mock` on Vercel production — the app will refuse to start.
